{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you, Elena. To answer Sofia's question: the forensic imaging review I completed yesterday was conducted entirely internally — no outside forensic expert was involved. That means the insurer's written consent requirement for engaging an outside expert has not been triggered by my work so far. If we do contemplate engaging an outside expert going forward, we would of course need to obtain the insurer's written consent first, per Sofia's report.

